# Wave W17-S (Route 129): lee sand — lee-shore sand: a pale calm shore sand under the crater\u2019s lee, fine sparse flecks lying quiet — the water turns here and the shore reads sheltered, the calm before the Driftlog corridor (design: the south-running sea under the crater\u2019s bulk, the lane bending gently south). Route 129\u2019s own sand — the fleet\u2019s palest, calmest sand: split from Route 128\u2019s cool deep-channel sand by brightness and from Route 127\u2019s kelp-shadowed sand by the missing green — nothing shades this shore.
